why we use SQLAlchemy in fast api??


Bro, the main reason we use SQLAlchemy with FastAPI is that FastAPI itself doesn't provide an ORM/database layer.
Think about Django first.
In Django
Django already gives you:

Django
  ↓
Django ORM
  ↓
Database

You can write:

Product.objects.all()
Product.objects.create(...)
Product.objects.filter(id=1)

You don't need another ORM because Django ORM is built into Django.

In FastAPI
FastAPI is mainly an API framework:

FastAPI
   ↓
??? 
   ↓
Database

FastAPI doesn't say:
"Use this ORM."
So you choose one.
A very common choice is:

FastAPI
   ↓
SQLAlchemy
   ↓
SQLite / PostgreSQL / MySQL


What exactly does SQLAlchemy give us?
1. It gives us an ORM
Instead of writing raw SQL:

SELECT * FROM products WHERE id = 1;

you can write:

product = db.query(Product).filter(Product.id == 1).first()

Instead of:

INSERT INTO products (name, price)
VALUES ('iPhone', 70000);

you can do:

product = Product(
    name="iPhone",
    price=70000
)

db.add(product)
db.commit()

SQLAlchemy translates your Python operations into SQL.
