now tell me the schemas and model thing in fast api

Haan bro. Ab Models vs Schemas ko ekdum clearly samajh le. Ye FastAPI mein starting mein sabse confusing part hota hai.
1. SQLAlchemy Model — Database ke liye
models/product.py

from sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, String, Float
from app.database import Base


class Product(Base):
    __tablename__ = "products"

    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    name = Column(String, nullable=False)
    description = Column(String, nullable=True)
    price = Column(Float, nullable=False)
    quantity = Column(Integer, nullable=False, default=0)

Ye database table ka blueprint hai.
Basically:

SQLAlchemy Model
       ↓
   Database
       ↓
products table

SQLite mein table roughly:

products
------------------------------------
id | name | description | price | quantity
------------------------------------
1  | iPhone | Apple phone | 70000 | 10
2  | AirPods | Earbuds | 20000 | 5

So SQLAlchemy model ka concern hai:
"Database mein data kaise store hoga?"

2. Pydantic Schema — API ke liye
schemas/product.py

from pydantic import BaseModel


class ProductCreate(BaseModel):
    name: str
    description: str
    price: float
    quantity: int

Ye database table nahi banata.
Ye API ko batata hai:
"Client se mujhe kis format ka data chahiye?"
For example client POST karega:

{
    "name": "iPhone",
    "description": "Apple phone",
    "price": 70000,
    "quantity": 10
}

Pydantic check karega:

name        → str    ✅
description → str    ✅
price       → float  ✅
quantity    → int    ✅

Agar:

{
    "name": "iPhone",
    "price": "hello",
    "quantity": "abc"
}

